title: Sign-in or secret prompt on an untrusted host
severity: high
score: 40
tags: phishing, credential-harvest
attack: T1566.002, T1583.001
description: A page asks for a password, a sign-in name, a one-time code, a card or a
  recovery phrase on a host that vouches for nothing: a free hosting tenant, a heavily
  abused TLD, a bare IP address or a domain registered less than 90 days ago. No brand
  needs to be recognised. Some real apps sign in on such hosts too, so on its own this
  is suspicious, not malicious.
---
// A top-level page (an open tab or a page seen earlier) that asks for a secret, on a host
// in untrusted_hosts (hosting/_shared.kql).
frames
| where top and prompt in ("password", "username", "otp", "seed", "payment")
| where host in (untrusted_hosts | project host)
| project url = substring(url, 0, 300), host, prompt
| take 5
